{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subject that broadcasts its current value and all subsequent values to multiple consumers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It can also handle completion events, including normal termination and failure with an error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This is an "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s CurrentValueSubject."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CurrentValueSubject"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Subscribing","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Subscribing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A consumer subscribes when its iterator is created, which is when a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for try await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop over the subject","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. It first receives the value that is current at that moment,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then every value sent afterwards, in order; values are buffered for it until it consumes them. Values sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before it subscribed are not replayed. A consumer that subscribes after completion receives only t